  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Add an option for multiple “Respawn planes”\nWith the addition of zero and negative gravity possibly brings the issue of floating away in other directions where the standard single respawn plane under the world wont be of any help. \nWe have had edge case issues of this as well in worlds/avatars where someone can sit on a chair and be thrown or picked up by themselves; as well as Udon worlds where you can “yeet” someone into precision errors. Adding more options for a world creator to use such as more “respawn directions” to keep players from getting flung or drifting too far off in specific directions, and help keep players in the playable area. \nThis can already be done in Udon but I feel with zero and negative gravity this could become more of an issue in the future and would be nice to have a default way to have this easily setup without creating your own Udon script or digging for a prefab.",
